Gibson, Fisk, Johnston, Halloran and Hunt…
but none were onto Jigsaw before the duo of

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.430
David Tapp and Stephen Sing.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.440
Welcome to Horror History,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.340
“my name jeff”

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.070
and in today’s lesson we’ll be analysing

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.329
a pair of the Metropolitan Police Department’s
finest, David Tapp and Stephen Sing.

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:49.039
Sing and Tapp play very important roles in
the bathroom game that took place in October

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:53.129
2004, but before we can get there, we’ve
got to study all the events that led up to

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:55.680
that point, so I’m gonna put the Horror
History screen now.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:00.370
David Tapp was born…

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.250
I don’t know probably in the 40s, I’m
not sure how old he’s supposed to be, but

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.560
we do know that his partner, Stephen Sing,
was born in 1976, because his age at the time

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.590
of death is stated to be 28 years old.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:16.869
“A raid that also resulted in the death
of Tapp’s partner, 28 year old Stephen Sing.”

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:20.189
Before the Jigsaw case, it seems they spend
most of their time dealing with low-level

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:21.340
street gangsters.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.700
One of the gangs they busted was called K2K.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.119
After locking them up, their territory was
still marked with graffiti, a lasting reminder

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.979
of the damage they caused to the community.

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:32.700
The first we see of Tapp and Sing investigating
the Jigsaw case was at the crime scene of

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.890
Paul in the Spring of 2004.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.229
They check things out with Detective Alison
Kerry, and I think her line suggests that

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:40.850
Paul may not have been the first victim that these
three encountered.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.229
“This one’s not fresh anymore.

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:43.979
At least three weeks out.”

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.120
But they must be pretty new to the Jigsaw
saga overall at this point.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.659
The younger of the two, Sing, looks like he’s
never smelled a corpse in decay before.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:54.159
Tapp on the other hand doesn’t seem distracted
by the stench and is able to fully focus on

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:58.090
the contents of the tape found at the crime
scene, wherein Jigsaw calls Paul out on acts

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.640
of self harm and tells him if he wants to
live, he’ll have to cut himself again, by

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.460
crawling through a cage filled with razor
wire to reach the door.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.220
I think one of the reasons Tapp and Sing work
well together is that their skillsets compliment

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:08.860
each other.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.500
For example, Tapp seems to have a greater
attention to detail.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.860
He’s the one to notice the Jigsaw piece
cut out of Paul’s shoulder, the origin of

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.870
the nickname that newspapers would begin using
to refer to the killer.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.860
At some point, Sing is shown going inside
the cage for a closer look.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.980
So I think Tapp, being the senior, calls the
shots, while Sing is the hands on guy.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.350
They aren’t able to gain any suspects from
the Razor Wire Trap, but in the meantime,

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.870
they are busy with other cases, and bring
in a pedo dentist, something that sounds like

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.060
it could be the subject of its own horror
movie.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.660
Not long after, the three of them investigated
the Flammable Jelly Trap, where a man named

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.560
Mark Wilson is tested by Jigsaw for faking
his illness.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.540
He’d been tasked with getting the combination
to a safe written on the wall of a dark room.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.280
His only source of light is a small candle,
and he’s covered in flammable jelly.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.540
Also the floor is covered in broken glass,
as if Jigsaw hired Link to come in and do his thing.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.660
Is there anything more satisfying than that?

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.660
No.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.810
No there is not.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:03.410
Tapp orders Kerry to have a pen light found
at the crime scene tested for fingerprints,

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.670
leading them to an oncologist named Dr. Lawrence
Gordon.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.650
They turn up at the Angel of Mercy Hospital
where Gordon works and asks him for his whereabouts

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.650
the previous night.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.550
When he’s unable to provide that information,
they ask him to come down to the police station.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:18.170
After initial hesitation, Gordon gives an
alibi: his mistress whom he was meeting in

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.050
secret at a seedy motel.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.620
Around that same time, a survivor of one of
Jigsaw’s games comes into the station to

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.500
file a police report, a woman by the name
of Amanda Young.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.880
The detectives are able to clear Gordon’s
name, but they ask him to stay a little bit longer

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.570
and listen to Amanda’s testimony, because
everyone is still confused by how Gordon’s

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.130
pen light ended up at the crime scene.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:39.210
She tells them that she’s actually grateful
to Jigsaw for his test helping her overcome

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.410
her drug addiction.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.110
Still not convinced that Gordon is innocent,
Detective Tapp becomes obsessed with the videotape

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.230
recovered from the room that Amanda had been
trapped in.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.460
For the next two weeks, he studies it over
and over, probably going through boxes and

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:55.130
boxes of delicious donuts, to the point that
Sing notices his partner delving into insanity.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:04:00.370
“Hey Tapp, I don’t mean for this to be
disrespectful… maybe you should find yourself

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.300
a girlfriend.”

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:05.400
Just then, Tapp notices something, that gives
him an epiphany about the possible whereabouts

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.280
of Jigsaw.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:10.260
He sees graffiti with the symbol of the gang,
K2K, who they’d busted before they Jigsaw

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:10.900
saga.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.640
Sing remembers that they had a small territory, only about four blocks, narrowing down their

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.100
search area considerably.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.680
Tapp also hears a fire alarm in the background
somehow.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.660
Honestly I always thought this was ridiculous.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.460
Play the clip.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.600
“Now listen to this….”

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.880
Faint audio: “Welcome to the Kill Count, where we tally
up the victims in all our favorite horror

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:32.380
movies.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.660
I’m James A Janisse and today we’re looking
at Saw...”

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.460
They’re able to get a list from the fire
department of every emergency in that neighborhood

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.900
over a two week period, and this further narrows
down the options to an old mannequin factory.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.920
“You think we have enough for a warrant
though?”

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.160
“Who said anything about a warrant?”

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.100
“Breakin the law!

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.280
Breaking the law!”

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.260
Inside they discover a model version of what
would be Jigsaw’s next game, though Sing

00:04:53.261 --> 00:04:54.770
and Tapp did not know it yet.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.530
They do know they are in the right place however,
because they discover Billy the Puppet, the same

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.630
avatar used in the Amanda Young tape.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.760
Tapp uncovers a man being held captive.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:06.820
They were about to experience one of Jigsaw’s
traps first hand, but what they did not anticipate

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.240
was that they would be the ones who

