00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.860
As Jigsaw could be heard coming in on the
noisy elevator down the hall, the two

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.940
partners had different ideas of how to handle
the situation.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.720
Sing, the younger less experienced one is
excited to catch the increasingly infamous

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.010
serial killer, but Tapp had the foresight
to wait so that they could catch him in the

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:54.370
act and maybe learn a thing or two about him
before putting him away.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:58.170
If they could, they may be better prepared
to pin all the killings on him in court.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:01.760
These viewpoints also go back to their roles
I mentioned earlier with Tapp being the head

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.340
and Sing being the hands.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:07.260
They hide and watch as the hooded figure goes
to investigate the disturbance in his latest

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:07.860
prisoner.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:12.000
Their mistake here is being unprepared, as
they vastly underestimate Jigsaw’s intelligence

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.190
and ability to think ahead and anticipate.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:18.000
Jigsaw has been expecting them, and although
he doesn’t show it, he knows they are in

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.190
the room as soon as he comes in, so when they
come out to arrest him, Jigsaw puts his plan

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.960
into action, stepping on a button that
starts the trap.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.860
A pair of drills close in on the prisoner’s
head, and Jigsaw tells Sing and Tapp that

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.460
they must choose what’s more important,
making the arrest, or saving the life of another

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:32.960
man.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.680
While Sing tries to figure out which key to
use, Tapp makes sure that Jigsaw doesn’t

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:40.440
escape, so in the eyes of Jigsaw, Sing has
passed this test by showing compassion for

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.590
human life, and Tapp has failed, due to his
obsession with catching Jigsaw.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:48.180
Sing is able to stop the progress of the drills
by shooting them, but Jigsaw pulls a blade

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.490
and cuts Tapp’s throat before making his
escape.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.770
Sing tells his partner that he’ll come back
for him, not realizing that he is still under

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:57.350
Jigsaw’s judgement, and by chasing after
Jigsaw while his friend continues to suffer,

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.710
he’s making the same mistake that Tapp made
just moments before.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:04.090
He chases Jigsaw downstairs into a hallway,
and orders him to freeze.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.380
When Jigsaw continues to flee, he fires a
shot, and Jigsaw hits the floor.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.930
I’ve said throughout this video that Tapp
and Sing’s skillsets compliment each other,

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:15.360
but with Tapp no longer there to offer his
wisdom, Sing makes one rookie mistake,

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.860
and this time, it’s fatal.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.100
He fails to realize that this whole scenario
was a little too easy.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:24.660
Would the greatest criminal mind the city
has ever seen just walk out into open fire

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.410
like that with no protection?

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:30.419
Sing doesn’t consider the idea that Jigsaw
was faking it, and this mistake leads him

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:34.800
right into the next trap, a fishing wire obscured
by some Halloween store cobwebs, which sets

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.439
off a row of loaded weapons hidden above.

00:08:37.439 --> 00:08:41.079
All Sing had to do to pass Jigsaw’s test
would have been to stay back and help his

00:08:41.079 --> 00:08:44.999
suffering partner, but his thirst to take
down the man they’ve been looking for outweighs

00:08:44.999 --> 00:08:47.100
the magnitude of a moral high ground.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.170
Tapp struggles down the stairs just in time
to see Jigsaw get up and walk away from the

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.800
remains of Sing’s now lifeless body.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:58.170
If there’s a moment that defines David Tapp;
that dictates his course of action from here

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:02.759
on out, it is the image of his trusted partner
Sing who had died trying to bring their greatest

00:09:02.759 --> 00:09:04.250
adversary to justice.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.899
To this point, he had shown signs of obsession
with the case, spending many hours studying

00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:13.249
the Amanda Young tape, but it was this moment
when the obsession turned from determination

00:09:13.249 --> 00:09:16.029
to ire and a deep yearning for revenge.

00:09:16.029 --> 00:09:18.389
This was the moment where Tapp went off the
deep end.

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:22.009
In the aftermath of this event, David was
discharged from the Metropolitan Police Force

00:09:22.009 --> 00:09:25.850
on the grounds of entering without a warrant,
so he ended up continuing to investigate on

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:26.560
his own.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.300
That summer, as the scar on this throat slowly
healed, he went deeper and deeper down the

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:34.180
rabbit hole, dedicating his life to finding
and stopping the man who killed his partner

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.790
and attempted to take his life.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:40.009
Due to Jigsaw’s oversized hood and robes,
Tapp never got a good look at his face, and

00:09:40.009 --> 00:09:43.100
thus, still suspected Lawrence Gordon as his
primary suspect.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.639
He went out and rented himself an apartment
with an excellent view of Gordon’s home,

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:50.120
which he would use to spy on the doctor and
his family over the course of the next five

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:50.800
months.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:55.160
The apartment was also used as a headquarters
which is absolutely littered with newspaper

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.920
clippings, tapes, photographs and other documents.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.819
What little space he had left was designated
to takeout boxes and also this crazed picture

00:10:01.819 --> 00:10:06.079
of Rick Sanchez for some reason… perhaps
just to depict Tapp’s manic state and complete

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.820
loss of touch with reality at the hands of
his fixation.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.320
In October of 2004, Tapp is starting to run
out of leads, and hires a photographer named

00:10:13.329 --> 00:10:17.319
Adam Stanheight to follow Gordon around while
he’s out and about, hoping he can snap some

00:10:17.319 --> 00:10:19.540
evidence proving that the doctor is the killer.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:23.369
He uses a pseudonym, “Bob”, and pays Adam
$200 each night.

00:10:23.369 --> 00:10:26.899
On the third night, Adam and Lawrence are
both captured and put into Jigsaw’s game

00:10:26.899 --> 00:10:30.559
in a dilapidated bathroom while Tapp watches
the window of Gordon’s home and notices

00:10:30.559 --> 00:10:33.480
a mysterious man in there while the doctor
is not home.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.580
He realizes that something is very wrong when
he hears gunshots.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:40.519
Even in his deteriorated mental state, his
goal is still to serve justice.

00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:44.500
He loads his weapon and runs across the street
to find Gordon’s wife, Alison in the midst

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.579
of a struggle with the man he had seen in
the window.

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:50.670
I think this is where Tapp finally realizes
that Lawrence Gordon is not the perpetrator

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.040
of these games and traps, he and his family
are victims of it.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.920
He battles with the captor, who channels his
inner Link and smashes a vase over Tapp’s

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.240
head and attempts to make his getaway.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.579
As soon as he is able to get back to his feet,
he goes after the man, who leads him to the

00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:04.579
location that Gordon and Adam are being held.

00:11:04.579 --> 00:11:08.360
At this point, Tapp must be pretty convinced
that he’s right on the tail of Jigsaw, and

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:10.569
doesn’t hold anything back in his fiery
pursuit.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:14.529
But as I’ve said over 69 times over the
course of this video, Tapp is just one half

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:15.769
of a two person team.

00:11:15.769 --> 00:11:19.540
He’s been working solo for five months,
but in this final chase, he misses his late

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.319
partner Sing more than ever.

00:11:21.319 --> 00:11:25.040
Because Sing was always the hands on guy,
the guy who would take those shots while Tapp

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.089
planned what to do next.

00:11:26.089 --> 00:11:29.509
But as Tapp was likely in his late 50s at
this point, he didn’t have the strength

00:11:29.509 --> 00:11:33.600
he once did, and at the end of a long chase,
Zepp is able to overpower him and do away

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.709
with the ex cop once and for all.

00:11:35.709 --> 00:11:39.619
That was the end of the buddy cop duo, the
first in a long line of police officers who

00:11:39.619 --> 00:11:41.730
would fall during Jigsaw’s active years.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:46.000
Nearly two years later, in April of 2006,
the officers are honored in a public police

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.860
ceremony and photographs of both Sing and
Tapp can be seen on the memorial.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:53.520
To be totally honest, I don’t really know why Tapp
is on there because he was no longer a cop

00:11:53.529 --> 00:11:56.739
when he died, and the location of the bathroom
wasn’t discovered until years later, so

00:11:56.739 --> 00:12:00.350
they wouldn’t have actually even found his
body yet… but he did contribute a lot of

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.759
information to the case, so I’ll let that
one slide.

00:12:02.759 --> 00:12:05.820
Now if you want more on Tapp, if you’re just
craving more Tapp,

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.240
then you’re probably an alcoholic--

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.600
*crowd booing*

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:12.119
No, but Tapp’s story does continue on in
Saw: The Video Game--

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.740
“I want to play a game.”

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.980
Yes, I know Jigsaw, but the video game is
not canon, it doesn’t count as a part of

00:12:18.989 --> 00:12:21.810
the story, so I’m not going to cover it
here on Horror History, because it would just

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:25.239
create problems with the timeline, but I’d
be open to playing it if that’s what you

00:12:25.239 --> 00:12:26.239
want to see.

00:12:26.239 --> 00:12:29.879
The basic gist of it is that Tapp survives
the gunshot, but finds himself in the reverse

00:12:29.879 --> 00:12:33.670
bear trap, and once he gets out of it he has
to save all these people from traps, and then

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:37.279
at the end he chases down Jigsaw and is faced
once again with the decision he had to make

00:12:37.279 --> 00:12:41.319
at the mannequin factory, either get the victims
to safety or continue to go after Jigsaw.

00:12:41.319 --> 00:12:44.819
Then there’s also a sequel to the video
game which involves Tapp’s son, that he

00:12:44.819 --> 00:12:48.709
apparently has, but I think that’s really
getting off topic and the deathbell’s about

00:12:48.709 --> 00:12:50.949
to ring so I think this is gonna be class
dismissed.

00:12:50.949 --> 00:12:53.769
For the homework, just make sure you like
this video and let me know in the comments

00:12:53.769 --> 00:12:56.680
which character you’d like to see me cover
next on Horror History.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:13:00.420
And as always check out the playlist on the
left to see the histories of other Saw characters

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.679
and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:13:04.679 --> 00:13:07.790
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:10.019
Assuming we both survive.

